YAAP - Winkle-Wiz-Hum-Mal-Cha ascended to demigod-hood

Finally I get ascension number 2!!  After a half-dozen or so "close
but no cigar" attempts over the past couple of years since my first
ascension, I get another one.

This was a nothing special, no conduct ascension.  I just wanted to
win.  The game was relatively routine.  I just took my time gaining
experience, learning spells, and tackling the various challenges of
the dungeon.

Highlights, Thoughts, etc. 

1)  I believe that my previous close calls were lost because I was
burdened when the onslaught of monsters began (either in the Astral
Planes or below).  This time I made sure that I was burdened as few
turns as possible.  Particularly when I got to the planes.

2)  The first scroll Winkle found was magic missile.  I believe this
was key to Winkle surviving the early and middle parts of the game. 
Magic missile is a killer (pun intended) spell.

3)  Winkle found +oId and +oRC fairly early.  These really helped too.

4)  Winkle used his quarterstaff, which he got to +6 (+5 at the end
due to an R), to great advantage throughout the game.  That
quarterstaff and Magicbane were his primary weapons.

5)  Winkle's armor included:

+4 Hawaiian shirt
+4 CoMR
+5 SDSM
+4 speed boots (I made sure to have these for the end game.  I used +4
ww boots otherwise)
+4 GoDex
+3 (or 4) Cornathaum

6) Winkle wore a "oLS, which saved him at some point early in the
game.  (I don't remember the details as I worked on this game for 10
days.)

7) A hairy situation occured on the Plane of Fire when 3 to 5 Archons
appearred and almost flooded the level with monsters.  I never really
got close to death; but I wondered if I would ever be able to get to
the portal (which I found when one of the monsters stepped on it)  I
used charm monster spell, \oTele, and =oConflict to work my way to the
portal.  I didn't want to resort to the ring of conflict.  However I
wanted to win more than abide by that conduct.  So I put it on.  It
kept a good number of the monsters busy and was key to getting through
them to the portal.

8) The Astral Plane wasn't as bad as the last couple of times I died
there.  I think that \oTele helped there (and the =oConflict which I
still had on).  I went to the altar on the left first, it was lawful. 
I then fought my way to the altar on the right and it was chaotic!!

9) I wanted to bring up a bag of jewels.  I had id'ed all the valuable
ones.  However, I was concerned about being burdened so I left them in
the dungeon.

10) Miscellaneous stats:

11 genocides -- all h's (I hate mf's), all L's
15 wishes -- mainly magic markers, ?oCharging, ww boots, +'s of dig,
magic mapping, charm monster (which I never found)

5936508 points

My max HP was 261
My AC was -33 (or -36 I forget)

Winkle killed Rodney 11 times (finger of death!!)

That's all I can remember at the moment.  I'm just excited I finally
won after so many tries.  Maybe after another ascension or two (Think
positively!!) I will try to tackle some conduct challenges.

